  m_Name: Scene07_FAQ_2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OhmsLaw.DialogueLine
  id: Scene07_FAQ_2
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: A galvanometer detects electric current. Ohm's torsion galvanometer had a
    magnetic needle hanging on a thread; current in a nearby wire twisted the needle,
    and how far he had to twist the thread back told him how strong the current was.
    Our ammeter does that job today.
  ttsText: A galvanometer detects electric current. Ohm's torsion galvanometer had
    a magnetic needle hanging on a thread; current in a nearby wire twisted the needle,
    and how far he had to twist the thread back told him how strong the current was.
    Our ammeter does that job today.
